        "orario": "11:35",
        "timestamp": 1773916547,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. EU leaders pile pressure on Hungary's Orban to lift block on Ukraine loan Issued on: 19/03/2026 - 11:35 European Union leaders piled pressure on Hungarian Prime Minister Viktor Orban on Thursday to lift his blockade on a vital 90-billion-euro ($103 billion) EU loan to ​Ukraine to keep ‌up its fight against Russia's invasion. EU leaders agreed to the loan in December but Orban, who has ⁠cordial ties with Russia and has clashed with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy, blocked its implementation last month, citing a dispute over a war-damaged pipeline. FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports from Kyiv, Ukraine. Trump threatens to strike world's largest gas field if Iran attacks Qatar again 19/03/2026 Who is running Iran? Top leadership decimated by US-Israeli strikes 19/03/2026 Iraq caught in crossfire of Middle East war 19/03/2026 Dozens arrested in Dubai for allegedly filming the war 19/03/2026 French top diplomat to visit Beirut: Paris vows solidarity with Lebanon 19/03/2026 EU summit to focus on wars in the Middle East and Ukraine 19/03/2026 War in Ukraine: Kharkiv opera defies Russian bombardment 19/03/2026 Iran causes 'extensive' damage to Qatar gas hub, sparks Trump warning 19/03/2026 Inside Lebanon's emergency response as displacement crisis strains resources 19/03/2026"
